From 04a5e35ffd83373dd6e0e7b6766731bbd3c3922f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:28:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Migrate stuffsdrop into NS on Drizzle, with a rail +
 sidebar shell

Port every working page and API route from the Refine + Prisma stuffsdrop
app. Prisma is replaced by Drizzle (postgres-js); the schema mirrors the
Prisma-created tables exactly, so the existing database is used as-is.
Refine, antd and the Supabase data provider are gone; auth is plain
@supabase/ssr with a Next 16 proxy.ts session refresh.

The layout follows mcs-sdk: a top bar over a primary icon rail, a
secondary sidebar whose links follow the active rail section, the page,
and a notifications panel that pushes the page aside. Mobile gets a
floating nav pill.

Fixes along the way:
- the API trusted a user id from user_metadata, which users can set
  themselves; the User row is now looked up by Supabase id
- item detail no longer exposes delivery OTPs, or receiver contact
  details to anyone other than the giver and the requester
- item PATCH only accepts listing fields; /api/upload requires sign-in
- dead nav links now go to real pages: archive categories, settings,
  edit drop, forgot password, and garment/exchange cards
- top bar search filters All Stuffs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
