From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add a light theme modelled on mcs-sdk, with a theme
 switcher

Pages no longer hard-code the dark palette. Colours go through theme
tokens (background, card, surface-2..4, the fg-* text ramp, brand /
brand-ink), so every page works in both themes:

- light follows mcs-sdk: lavender-tinted off-white page, ink text, white
  cards with hairline borders and soft shadows, white active pills in the
  rail and sidebar
- dark keeps the stuffsdrop look: near-black canvas, white type, mint
- white-on-black buttons invert to black-on-white in light; mint stays
  the accent, with a deeper shade for mint text on light backgrounds

Theme is Light / Dark / System (default System) via next-themes, switched
from the account menu, Settings, or the mobile menu. The sign-in and
sign-up screens stay dark as standalone branded pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
